{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["# SQLite in the Browser sqlite3 🐘\n\nThis notebook demonstrates using Python's built-in `sqlite3` module to work with an in-memory SQLite database, all running inside your browser thanks to Pyodide."] 
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["import sqlite3\n","import pandas as pd\n", "\n", "print(f"SQLite version: {sqlite3.sqlite_version}")"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 1. Create an In-Memory Database and Table\n","We will create a database that exists only as long as this notebook is running."] 
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["# Create a connection to an in-memory database\n","con = sqlite3.connect(':memory:')\n","cur = con.cursor()\n", "\n", "# Create a table called 'products'\n","cur.execute(\"""CREATE TABLE products\n               (name TEXT, category TEXT, price REAL, stock INTEGER)\""")\n", "\n", "print("Database and 'products' table created successfully in memory.")"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 2. Insert Data\n","Let's add some data to our table."] 
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["# Data to be inserted\n","products_data = [\n","    ('Laptop', 'Electronics', 1200.50, 50),\n","    ('Coffee Mug', 'Kitchenware', 15.00, 200),\n","    ('Notebook', 'Stationery', 5.25, 500),\n","    ('Desk Chair', 'Furniture', 150.75, 100),\n","    ('Mouse', 'Electronics', 25.00, 300)\n", " ]\n", "\n","# Insert multiple records\n","cur.executemany("INSERT INTO products VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)", products_data)\n","con.commit()\n", "\n", "print(f"{len(products_data)} records inserted successfully.")"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 3. Query Data with SQL\n","Now we can run standard SQL queries on our data."] 
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["# Query all electronics products\n","res = cur.execute("SELECT name, price FROM products WHERE category = 'Electronics'")\n","electronics = res.fetchall()\n", "\n", "print("Electronic Products:")\n","for product in electronics:\n","    print(product)"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 4. Use with Pandas\n","The real power comes from integrating with other data science libraries like Pandas."] 
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["# Read the entire table into a pandas DataFrame\n","df = pd.read_sql_query("SELECT * FROM products", con)\n", "\n","# Close the connection\n","con.close()\n", "\n","display(df)"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["# Now you can use pandas to analyze and visualize the data\n","df.describe()"]
  }
 ],
